1.1.1: the terminal speaks Chinese, Jade names ULTRAKILL's enemies, and entering a world no longer stalls

The terminal's upgrade page is translated: names, effects and the about lines all
come from a language table keyed by the same strings the page already used, so a
Minecraft running in English shows exactly what it showed before. Chinese needs a
font ULTRAKILL does not ship - the shipped font has no CJK glyphs at all - so the
font pack is a separate download that sits next to the bridge dll. Without it the
terminal stays English and nothing else changes. zh_cn.json covers the Minecraft
side, 464 keys, including the settings screen, the boss setup screen and every
option value that used to be hardcoded English.

Jade shows an ULTRAKILL enemy's real name and its health, read from the enemy
itself rather than guessed from the Minecraft stand-in, which is what the mob
damage filter needed in order to list what it was filtering.

Entering a world used to stall for about a second. The stall was the navmesh
being baked for the first time on the frame the sandbox woke up; it is now baked
while Minecraft is still loading the world, so the frame that used to pay for it
is already past. The view is also handed over on the first teleport instead of at
level preparation, which is what made the window go black before V1 arrived.

The rest is smaller: the arm mesh is only exported while the arms are idle, so a
punch or a held item no longer bakes its pose into the skin; health caps at four
times V1's own full health instead of a flat number; the mod's keys get their own
category instead of sitting in Miscellaneous; the boss intro line names the
difficulty and the modifiers; fire on your own body actually goes out; and a
handful of interface strings that were assembled at runtime now resolve to real
translations.
